<title>GERMANY: Germany to convert debt to euros in 1999 - paper.</title>
<headline>Germany to convert debt to euros in 1999 - paper.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany is to convert its stock of debt from marks into euros from the start of 1999, the launch deadline for Europe's monetary union, the Handelsblatt newspaper said on Monday citing government sources.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the finance ministry had dropped its objections to an early conversion largely due to the example of France and the Netherlands, which have already announced plans to convert their debt to euros.</p>
<p>Full technical details had not yet been finalised, the paper said. No immediate confirmation of the report was available.</p>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel is understood to have discussed the debt conversion project at a meeting in Bonn with leading bankers last Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
